# Frontend React

- The standalone SPA lives in `frontend/`; use React 19, TypeScript, and Vite.
- `src/main.tsx` mounts the app and `src/App.tsx` composes the current page.
- Keep layout components in `src/components/layout`, page sections in `src/components/sections`, and reusable UI in `src/components/ui`.
- Colocate component CSS next to the component when following existing patterns.
- Static UI data can live in `src/data`; move it behind API calls when it becomes backend-owned data.
- Use `VITE_API_URL` from `frontend/.env` for backend API calls. Avoid hardcoded API hosts in components.
- Keep components functional and typed. Prefer small props interfaces near the component unless shared broadly.
- After frontend changes, run the smallest relevant check first:
  - `cd frontend && npm run lint`
  - `cd frontend && npm run format:check`
  - `cd frontend && npm test`
  - `cd frontend && npm run build`
- Docker/Makefile equivalents:
  - `make frontend-lint`
  - `make frontend-format`
  - `make frontend-test`
  - `make npm-build`
- Prefer Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests colocated as `*.test.ts(x)`.
